  ASSUMPTIONS / LIMITS
==========================================================================================
  1. Fundamental components (rate_differential, DXY, COT, news_clear)
     are UNAVAILABLE — no CSVs in backtest_data/fundamentals/.
     Score is normalized against available components only (technical + ICT).
     This inflates % scores vs. a full fundamental stack.

  2. Scores computed against available points only:
     Max points if all technical ICT available ≈ 100 pts (trend 15+OB 20+
     FVG 15+sweep 15+PD 10+OTE 10+RSI 10+ADX 10+EMA 5 = 110 pts max)
     Normalised to 100 → thresholds 50/55/65 behave differently vs live.

  3. Position sizing uses compounding 1% risk per trade on a $1000 balance.
     pnl_r from simulator → dollar_gain = equity × 0.01 × pnl_r.

  4. Entry fill requires M1 candle range to touch the entry_zone midpoint.
     Signals where price never reaches the zone = no-fill = excluded.

  5. Kill-zone windows: London (3 AM EST), NY (8 AM EST), London Close (10 AM).
     3 windows per trading day × ~520 trading days = theoretical max windows.

  6. Same-candle tie-breaking: protective stop wins over TP on same candle.

  7. TP1 closes 50% at +1R, moves SL to entry (breakeven), then ATR-based
     trailing stop on remaining 50% until TP2 (+2R) or time/trail-stop exit.

  8. Time stop: closes if still below −0.5R after session-based holding limit.

